// TestPackManifestAudioJoint — pack-manifest-audio task 5.1, the Tier-1 joint
// over the change's five cross-seam contracts, every hop a real instance (a
// real ffmpeg pack through the real enrich streams lane, the real tokenized
// /media serving surface, the real api router over real HTTP; no mocks).
// cmd/mellifera is package main and cannot be imported, so the thin-shell
// closures it owns are mirrored here in miniature (the pbNewWorld /
// gateNewServer house pattern): the PackItem closure (the D7 "pack: gate"
// line + the PackGate pre-check + the Codecs outcome), the descriptor closure
// (decision_log.go's playbackDescriptor incl. the "playback: descriptor" line
// with codecs_src), and the play verb (packOnPlay incl. legacyRepackOnPlay).
// The decisions those closures JOIN are the production functions: stream.Pack,
// stream.PackGate, stream.Classify, stream.Describe, orchestrator.OnPlay.
//
//   - (a) the rendition master's SERVED shape: exactly ONE EXT-X-STREAM-INF
//     video variant with CODECS; the audio renditions ONLY as EXT-X-MEDIA
//     members (unique NAMEs, exactly one DEFAULT=YES — the embedded audio,
//     AUTOSELECT on both), never as variants; the served bytes carry the
//     tokenized URIs (self-authorizing playlists).
//   - (b) the single-variant master's SERVED shape: one variant line whose
//     CODECS names video+audio over the rend0/ media playlist, play URL
//     unchanged — and the PARTIAL build (head-first, observed mid-run through
//     a task-sanctioned tail-phase gate around the real ffmpeg) serves the
//     SAME master bytes before the tail merge completes.
//   - (c) the finding-B read side: a namespace predating the codec record over
//     the real Matroska fact shape answers the composed hvc1/mp4a strings with
//     the decision line naming codecs_src=legacy.
//   - (d) the pack flow line sequence over a real job: "pack: gate" then
//     "streams: pack published", one line per moment, no per-segment lines,
//     INV4 (no token, no play URL).
//   - (e) the lazy repack-on-play (rule-versioned): a stale item (hand-laid
//     valid flat build, version-free namespace = v0) answers POST /play with
//     exactly ONE repack enqueued — the old build serving while it runs, the
//     repacked build replacing it with a fresh nonce carrying the composed
//     master and the current rule version — and a second POST /play enqueues
//     nothing; a v1 boolean-true seed re-heals exactly once; a
//     current-version seed never enqueues.
//
// The tail-phase gate: afterHead is an unexported stream field, so the joint
// widens the head-first window hermetically instead — the pack service's
// FFmpeg points at a wrapper script that lets the head phase through and
// BLOCKS the tail invocation (its args carry -ss) until the test releases it.
// The rename of the partial build happens before packTail starts, so the
// started marker fires exactly when the partial build is published; nothing
// polls in the test and nothing races. Coverage referenced, not re-proven:
// the master composer units (stream/master_test.go), the flow vocabulary
// units (stream/pack_flow_log_test.go), the legacy-repack decision units
// (cmd/mellifera/playback_gate_test.go), the version persist
// (enrich/streams_test.go).
